## Validation Contexts

`ApplicationFormValidations#validate_flow(FlowClass)` introspects the flow and auto-generates a constant for each page name (e.g., `Flow::NAME`, `Flow::DATE_OF_BIRTH`). Consumers declare standard Rails validations scoped to these constants using `on:`. The controller then calls `record.valid?(Flow::PAGE_NAME)` inside each `update_<page>` action, so only the fields relevant to that page are validated on each step:

```ruby
class LeaveApplicationForm < Strata::ApplicationForm
  include Strata::Flows::ApplicationFormValidations
  validate_flow LeaveApplicationFlow

  validates :applicant_name_first, presence: true, on: Flow::NAME
  validates :date_of_birth_date, presence: true, on: Flow::DATE_OF_BIRTH
end
```

This keeps validations co-located with the model while still running them one page at a time during the multi-step flow.
